<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;JEANNE MAINDRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jeanne Maindron is a French woman who risked her life to hide Jewish families during World War II and was later honored with the Royal Order of the Seraphim and the title of Righteous Among the Nations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jeanne Maindron is a person whose bravery and selflessness are highlighted as a reminder of standing up for what is right in the face of danger."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOPHIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sophie is Jeanne Maindron's great-niece who visits her in the parlor and shows interest in the story of the beautiful box."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCH COUNTRYSIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French countryside is where Jeanne Maindron lived and performed her acts of bravery during the war."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL ORDER OF THE SERAPHIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Order of the Seraphim is the highest honor given by the Swedish government to Jeanne Maindron for her bravery during the war."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGHTEOUS AMONG THE NATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Righteous Among the Nations is an honor bestowed by the State of Israel to non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust."&lt;SEP&gt;"Righteous Among the Nations is an organization that recognizes individuals for their acts of bravery and selflessness during times of danger."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YAD VASHEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yad Vashem is the World Holocaust Remembrance Center in Jerusalem that recognizes and documents the actions of Righteous Among the Nations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYON, FRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lyon, France is where Jeanne Maindron resided and performed her acts of bravery during the war."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAZI REGIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Nazi regime is the oppressive force that persecuted Jewish people during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweden is the country that bestowed the Royal Order of the Seraphim upon Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israel is the country that bestowed the title of Righteous Among the Nations upon Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RABBI ISRAEL MEIR LAU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rabbi Israel Meir Lau is the Chairman of the Yad Vashem Council and speaks about Jeanne Maindron's bravery."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. ROBERT ROZETT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Robert Rozett is the Director of the Yad Vashem Libraries and speaks about Jeanne Maindron's bravery."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TANTE JEANNE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tante Jeanne is another way to refer to Jeanne Maindron, used by Sophie in the conversation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACARONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FOOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Macarons are delicate pastries that Sophie and Jeanne enjoy while reminiscing."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The parlor is the cozy room in Jeanne Maindron's home where she sits and reminisces with Sophie."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDISH GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Swedish government is the entity that bestowed the Royal Order of the Seraphim upon Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDISH AMBASSADOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Swedish ambassador is the individual who delivered the Royal Order of the Seraphim to Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING OF SWEDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The King of Sweden is the individual who wrote the letter of thanks to Jeanne Maindron within the Royal Order of the Seraphim."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JEWISH FAMILIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jewish families are the individuals Jeanne Maindron hid during the war."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FALSE IDENTIFICATION PAPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"False identification papers are the documents Jeanne Maindron helped obtain to protect Jewish families."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAVENDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lavender is the scent that wafts from the box containing the Royal Order of the Seraphim."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERAPHIM WINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SYMBOL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seraphim wings are the symbol depicted on the Royal Order of the Seraphim."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ornate box on the mantle contains the Royal Order of the Seraphim and is a focal point of the story."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;26,000 INDIVIDUALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"26,000 individuals have been recognized by the Righteous Among the Nations program for their acts of bravery and selflessness."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1963&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Righteous Among the Nations program was established in 1963, marking the beginning of its recognition of individuals for their acts of bravery."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HATRED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hatred is a concept that continues to pose a threat in the world, contrasting with the positive actions of individuals like Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTOLERANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intolerance is another concept that continues to pose a threat in the world, contrasting with the positive actions of individuals like Jeanne Maindron."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDING UP FOR WHAT IS RIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standing up for what is right is a concept that Jeanne Maindron exemplifies, highlighting the importance of moral courage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVERWHELMING DANGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Overwhelming danger is a concept that Jeanne Maindron faced, emphasizing the severity of the threats she confronted."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Legacy is a concept that Jeanne Maindron's actions will leave behind, inspiring future generations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Generations refer to future people who will be inspired by Jeanne Maindron's legacy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0209</data>
    </node>
